---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const schools = [
  { name: 'Pyro', color: 'var(--pyro)', text: 'Fire. Direct, punishing damage from the front line.' },
  { name: 'Frost', color: 'var(--frost)', text: 'Ice. Shields, slows, and control of the board.' },
  { name: 'Storm', color: 'var(--storm)', text: 'Lightning. Fast strikes that chain across adjacent hexes.' },
  { name: 'Verdant', color: 'var(--verdant)', text: 'Growth. Healing and wards that keep allies standing.' },
  { name: 'Geo', color: 'var(--geo)', text: 'Stone. Tough, positional play that reshapes the fight.' },
  { name: 'Umbral', color: 'var(--umbral)', text: 'Shadow. Tricks, drains, and an edge on any ground.' },
];
---
<Base title="Home" description="Tomebound Tactics — a mobile PvP strategy game where elemental wizards battle on a 61-hex board and learn spells by studying real books.">
  <span class="badge">In development</span>
  <h1>The game that levels you up for reading real books.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Tomebound Tactics is a mobile PvP strategy game. Elemental wizards battle on a board of sixty-one hexes — and they grow stronger by studying real books, one ISBN at a time.</p>

  <video class="hero" src="/teaser.mp4" poster="/emblem.png" controls preload="metadata" playsinline>
    Your browser does not support the video tag. <a href="/teaser.mp4">Watch the teaser</a>.
  </video>
  <p class="muted">First look: the board assembles, the shrines ignite, and a wizard opens the book to learn a new spell.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Scan a book.</strong> Point your phone camera at a book's ISBN. The book's original publication year sets your wizard's rank, and its study grants a skill — a page of the spellbook, once per wizard, ever.</li>
    <li><strong>Study once a day.</strong> Each wizard may study one book per day. The Daily Study Rule keeps the game about reading, not grinding.</li>
    <li><strong>Battle on the hexes.</strong> Wizards fight only from adjacent hexes, on a randomly generated sixty-one hex board with three shrines. Position is everything.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Six schools of wizardry</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {schools.map((s) => (
      <div class="card school" style={`border-top-color: ${s.color}`}>
        <h3 style={`color: ${s.color}`}>{s.name}</h3>
        <p>{s.text}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Epochs, not seasons</h2>
  <p>The game runs in eight-week epochs. Each epoch has a name, a storyline chapter unlocked by community milestones, and a canon of featured books. When an epoch ends, its abilities rotate to the Archive after two epochs — the Fading Rule — so the game keeps moving. The launch epoch will be called <strong>Alchemist Reign</strong>.</p>

  <h2>Never pay to win</h2>
  <p>Money buys cosmetics — skins, wands, spirit animals — and nothing that touches progression. Featured Tomes, the game's sponsorships, buy efficiency and certainty for a study, never extra power. A sponsor's book can be featured; it can never be stronger.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0">Get notified at launch</h3>
    <p>One email when the launch epoch opens, and one per epoch after that. Nothing else.</p>
    <!-- Newsletter: replace YOUR_LIST_ID with the Buttondown list ID once the list is created. See README. -->
    <form class="newsletter" action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/YOUR_LIST_ID" method="post">
      <label for="email" class="muted" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px">Email address</label>
      <input id="email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required />
      <button type="submit">Notify me</button>
    </form>
    <p class="muted">Newsletter signup opens once the mailing list is connected — see the README for the one-line setup.</p>
  </div>

  <p>
    <a class="btn" href="/libraries/">For libraries</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/sponsors/">For publishers</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/press/">Press kit</a>
  </p>
</Base>
